		{"id":"be9abb7d9e068da1","type":"text","text":"\n\n\n## 🧭 **C Language Sikhne ke Steps (Step-by-Step Guide for Beginners to Advanced)**\n\n---\n\n### 🩵 **Step 1: Samajh C Language kya hai**\n\n**Goal:** Programming world ka base samajhna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- C kya hai?\n    \n- C ka use kaha hota hai (embedded, OS, games, compilers)\n    \n- C program ka structure\n    \n- How code executes (Compile → Link → Run)\n    \n\n💡 **Example:**\n\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    printf(\"Hello, World!\");\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 💙 **Step 2: Basics – Syntax aur Building Blocks**\n\n**Goal:** Basic grammar of C samajhna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Keywords, Identifiers, Variables\n    \n- Data Types (int, float, char, double)\n    \n- Input/Output: `printf()` & `scanf()`\n    \n- Operators (Arithmetic, Relational, Logical, Assignment, Increment/Decrement)\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Write a program to add two numbers\n    \n- Find area of circle\n    \n- Convert Celsius to Fahrenheit\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💜 **Step 3: Control Statements (Decision Making)**\n\n**Goal:** Program ko smart banana — conditions ke hisaab se kaam kare.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- `if`, `else`, `else if`\n    \n- `switch` statement\n    \n- `goto` (avoid karna best hai 😅)\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Check if number is even or odd\n    \n- Find the largest among three numbers\n    \n- Make a calculator using switch case\n    \n\n---\n\n### ❤️ **Step 4: Loops (Repetition Mastery)**\n\n**Goal:** Code ko repeat karwana bina likhe.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- `for`, `while`, `do-while`\n    \n- Loop control: `break`, `continue`\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Print 1 to 100\n    \n- Print table of any number\n    \n- Print factorial of a number\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💚 **Step 5: Functions**\n\n**Goal:** Code ko divide karna aur reuse karna seekhna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Function syntax, parameters, return values\n    \n- Call by Value & Call by Reference\n    \n- Recursion (function calling itself)\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Find factorial using recursion\n    \n- Find GCD of two numbers\n    \n- Create a menu-driven calculator using functions\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💛 **Step 6: Arrays**\n\n**Goal:** Ek variable me multiple values store karna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- 1D Array\n    \n- 2D Array (Matrix)\n    \n- Array operations: searching, sorting\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Find maximum element in array\n    \n- Reverse an array\n    \n- Add two matrices\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🧡 **Step 7: Strings**\n\n**Goal:** Character data handle karna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Declaration and initialization\n    \n- String functions (`strlen`, `strcpy`, `strcmp`, `strcat`)\n    \n- Manual string operations\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Find length of string (without `strlen`)\n    \n- Compare two strings\n    \n- Count vowels and consonants\n    \n\n---\n\n### ❤️‍🔥 **Step 8: Pointers (Memory Understanding)**\n\n**Goal:** Memory me data ka control lena — C ka heart ❤️\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Basics of pointers\n    \n- Pointer arithmetic\n    \n- Pointers with arrays, strings, and functions\n    \n- Double pointers\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Swap two numbers using pointers\n    \n- Print array using pointers\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💜 **Step 9: Structures & Unions**\n\n**Goal:** Complex data handle karna (like objects in C).\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Define & access structures\n    \n- Array of structures\n    \n- Nested structures\n    \n- Difference between structure & union\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Create a student record system\n    \n- Store and print employee details\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🖤 **Step 10: File Handling**\n\n**Goal:** Data ko permanent banana (save in files).\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- File operations (`fopen`, `fprintf`, `fscanf`, `fclose`)\n    \n- Read/Write files\n    \n- Append data\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Write a program to store student marks in a file\n    \n- Read and display file content\n    \n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ **Step 11: Dynamic Memory Allocation**\n\n**Goal:** Runtime memory management samajhna.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- `malloc()`, `calloc()`, `realloc()`, `free()`\n    \n- Handling memory leaks\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Create a dynamic array\n    \n- Reallocate memory for growing data\n    \n\n---\n\n### 💫 **Step 12: Data Structures using C**\n\n**Goal:** Logic-building aur placement-level coding.\n\n#### 📘 Topics:\n\n- Linked List (Singly, Doubly)\n    \n- Stack, Queue\n    \n- Trees (Basic Understanding)\n    \n- Sorting and Searching Algorithms\n    \n\n💡 **Practice:**\n\n- Implement stack using array\n    \n- Implement queue using linked list\n    \n- Perform binary search in array\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🧠 **Step 13: Mini Projects**\n\n**Goal:** Apni knowledge ko real-world me use karna.\n\n#### 💡 Project Ideas:\n\n- Student Record System\n    \n- Simple Banking System\n    \n- File-based To-do List\n    \n- Library Management System\n    \n- Console Snake Game 🎮\n    \n\n---\n\n### 🚀 **Step 14: Practice & Mastery**\n\n**Goal:** Confidence build karna and competitive coding me entry.\n\n#### 💻 Practice Platforms:\n\n- [Programiz](https://www.programiz.com/c-programming)\n    \n- [HackerRank – C Track](https://www.hackerrank.com/domains/tutorials/10-days-of-c)\n    \n- [CodeChef](https://www.codechef.com/)\n    \n- [LeetCode (Easy Section)](https://leetcode.com/)\n    \n\n---\n\n### 📅 **Bonus: Daily Study Plan (Simple 1-Month)**\n\n|Week|Focus|Practice|\n|---|---|---|\n|1|Basics + Control + Loops|15–20 easy programs|\n|2|Functions + Arrays + Strings|25–30 programs|\n|3|Pointers + Structures + Files|10 small projects|\n|4|DSA + Real Projects|Build 2 projects|\n\n---\n\nAayush, agar tu chahe to main isi **step-by-step C learning roadmap** ko ek **printable PDF guide** me convert kar du —  \n✅ Har step ke short notes  \n✅ Practice tasks  \n✅ Example codes  \n✅ Progress tracker table\n\nBata — PDF **Hinglish me** banau ya **Pure English** me?  \n(Main usi format me bana ke tujhe complete C Language Study Guide dedunga 📘🔥)","x":-12240,"y":-212,"width":480,"height":449},
